Example to think about: "Italian food" and "pasta and risotto" — one contains the word, the other doesn't, but they're about the same topic.

--------------- A6 -----------------
that query in SQL search for the word "pizza" while vector index will search for words from the same category.
SQL doesn't understand meaning, it only checks for a certain text, vector index search for similarity.

